1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,445
Hi, I am Dhrumil Shah,
and this video is

2
00:00:02,445 --> 00:00:04,556
about Mycroft Phase
4, where I added

3
00:00:04,556 --> 00:00:06,901
market-regime discovery
and regime-aware

4
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:09,364
thresholds so the system
reports where its

5
00:00:09,364 --> 00:00:11,650
forecasts hold up,
instead of one score

6
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:13,147
for every market.

7
00:00:13,147 --> 00:00:15,696
Phase 3 ended with
an honest result.

8
00:00:15,696 --> 00:00:17,155
Across a hundred
and twenty

9
00:00:17,155 --> 00:00:18,885
tickers, five-day
direction came

10
00:00:18,885 --> 00:00:20,436
out close to
a coin flip.

11
00:00:20,436 --> 00:00:23,064
One number, for every
market condition.

12
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:25,148
That single number
hides something.

13
00:00:25,148 --> 00:00:26,868
A calm market
and a crash are

14
00:00:26,868 --> 00:00:28,314
not the same problem.

15
00:00:28,314 --> 00:00:30,126
Phase 4 asks
whether the model's

16
00:00:30,126 --> 00:00:31,994
weakness depends
on the regime it

17
00:00:31,994 --> 00:00:33,457
is predicting in.

18
00:00:33,457 --> 00:00:35,394
The input is unchanged.

19
00:00:35,394 --> 00:00:37,377
One hundred and
eighty-four thousand

20
00:00:37,377 --> 00:00:39,416
rows, one hundred
and twenty tickers,

21
00:00:39,416 --> 00:00:42,426
January twenty-twenty to
February twenty-twenty-six.

22
00:00:42,426 --> 00:00:44,610
Same data, new question.

23
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:46,583
The pipeline
gains a layer.

24
00:00:46,583 --> 00:00:48,859
Daily prices become
a market table; the

25
00:00:48,859 --> 00:00:51,193
market table becomes
regimes; the regime

26
00:00:51,193 --> 00:00:53,469
label joins the
features; and the model

27
00:00:53,469 --> 00:00:57,004
learns a separate decision
threshold for each regime.

28
00:00:57,004 --> 00:00:58,717
First, I collapse
every ticker

29
00:00:58,717 --> 00:01:00,116
into one row per day.

30
00:01:00,116 --> 00:01:02,639
Market return,
cross-sectional volatility,

31
00:01:02,639 --> 00:01:05,042
median twenty-day
return and volatility,

32
00:01:05,042 --> 00:01:07,205
advance rate, and
rolling twenty-day

33
00:01:07,205 --> 00:01:08,847
volatility and momentum.

34
00:01:08,847 --> 00:01:10,374
Seven numbers
that describe

35
00:01:10,374 --> 00:01:11,834
the whole market.

36
00:01:11,834 --> 00:01:13,837
Then K-means
splits those days

37
00:01:13,837 --> 00:01:15,239
into four regimes.

38
00:01:15,239 --> 00:01:17,460
The clustering is fit
only on the training

39
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,417
dates and then
applied forward, so no

40
00:01:19,417 --> 00:01:21,256
future day shapes
the clusters.

41
00:01:21,256 --> 00:01:22,892
Each cluster
gets a readable

42
00:01:22,892 --> 00:01:24,735
name from its centroid.

43
00:01:24,735 --> 00:01:25,816
Here is the map.

44
00:01:25,816 --> 00:01:27,629
Stressed bear is
almost entirely

45
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:30,492
the early twenty-twenty
crash, twenty-four days.

46
00:01:30,492 --> 00:01:32,816
High volatility,
ninety-seven.

47
00:01:32,816 --> 00:01:34,681
The market spends
most of its life

48
00:01:34,681 --> 00:01:36,162
in calm bull,
eight hundred

49
00:01:36,162 --> 00:01:38,082
twenty-one days,
or sideways mixed,

50
00:01:38,082 --> 00:01:39,898
five hundred fifty-four.

51
00:01:39,898 --> 00:01:42,510
The model is an Extra
Trees classifier over

52
00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:45,182
nineteen price and volume
features, plus the

53
00:01:45,182 --> 00:01:46,901
regime identifier
itself.

54
00:01:46,901 --> 00:01:49,087
Train, validation
and test are split by

55
00:01:49,087 --> 00:01:51,328
date, and missing
values are filled with

56
00:01:51,328 --> 00:01:53,061
training medians only.

57
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:54,907
The headline is
still honest.

58
00:01:54,907 --> 00:01:57,243
Test ROC-AUC is
point five one eight,

59
00:01:57,243 --> 00:01:59,642
and the Brier score
is point two five,

60
00:01:59,642 --> 00:02:01,546
what a coin
flip gives you.

61
00:02:01,546 --> 00:02:03,228
Regime awareness
did not make

62
00:02:03,228 --> 00:02:04,946
the model predictive.

63
00:02:04,946 --> 00:02:06,355
But split it
by regime and

64
00:02:06,355 --> 00:02:07,585
something shows up.

65
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,434
In high
volatility, AUC is

66
00:02:09,434 --> 00:02:10,772
point five four.

67
00:02:10,772 --> 00:02:13,018
Sideways mixed,
point five two.

68
00:02:13,018 --> 00:02:15,522
In calm bull, the most
common regime, it is

69
00:02:15,522 --> 00:02:17,469
point four nine,
below chance.

70
00:02:17,469 --> 00:02:19,377
The model is least
useful exactly

71
00:02:19,377 --> 00:02:21,323
when the market
is quiet.

72
00:02:21,323 --> 00:02:23,603
Permutation
importance agrees.

73
00:02:23,603 --> 00:02:25,343
The regime
identifier is the

74
00:02:25,343 --> 00:02:27,393
single most useful
feature, by an

75
00:02:27,393 --> 00:02:28,774
order of magnitude.

76
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:30,780
Most technical
indicators contribute

77
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:32,729
nothing, or
slightly hurt.

78
00:02:32,729 --> 00:02:34,449
So the thresholds adapt.

79
00:02:34,449 --> 00:02:36,837
Each regime gets its
own cut-off, tuned on

80
00:02:36,837 --> 00:02:39,224
validation for balanced
accuracy, and only

81
00:02:39,224 --> 00:02:41,555
names that clear it
by eight points enter

82
00:02:41,555 --> 00:02:42,835
the research queue.

83
00:02:42,835 --> 00:02:44,487
On the latest
day, a calm bull

84
00:02:44,487 --> 00:02:46,363
day, two names
qualified.

85
00:02:46,363 --> 00:02:47,891
Phase 4's
accomplishment is

86
00:02:47,891 --> 00:02:49,166
not a better score.

87
00:02:49,166 --> 00:02:50,911
It is a system
that knows where

88
00:02:50,911 --> 00:02:52,406
it is weak and says so.

89
